{"id":"n-20261015-54mc3z","category":"tech","display_title":"Zelda Ocarina of Time Switch 2 Remake","display_title_he":"חידוש זלדה אוקרינה של הזמן לנינטנדו סוויץ' 2","short_summary":"Nintendo is launching a richly detailed 4K remake of the 1998 classic The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time for the Nintendo Switch 2.","english_level":"C1","words":424,"reading_time":3,"image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a4/The_Legend_of_Zelda_Ocarina_of_Time_Master_Quest.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","credit":"Kigsz · Public domain","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Legend_of_Zelda_Ocarina_of_Time_Master_Quest.png"},"sources":[{"name":"The Guardian","domain":"theguardian.com","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/games/2026/oct/14/the-legend-of-zelda-ocarina-of-time-preview-4k-era-switch-2-remake","title":"The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time preview – Link faces his scariest challenge yet: the 4K era","published_at":"2026-10-14T13:00:02.000Z"},{"name":"NPR","domain":"npr.org","url":"https://www.npr.org/2026/10/14/nx-s1-5961483/preview-zelda-ocarina-of-time-remake-switch-2","title":"Hands-on with the Ocarina of Time remake, the most ornate Zelda game ever made","published_at":"2026-10-14T13:00:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-14T13:00:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-15T06:04:05.676Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Nintendo is preparing to release a lavish 4K remake of its 1998 classic video game, The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time, for the upcoming Nintendo Switch 2. According to recent hands-on previews, the title is scheduled to debut on November 5, arriving just two weeks before the meteoric arrival of Grand Theft Auto VI. This timing places the wholesome family-friendly fantasy adventure as a notable holiday counterweight to modern-day crime epics, standing out against the glitzy violence of Rockstar Games' release. Furthermore, the launch arrives just ahead of the Zelda franchise's upcoming big-screen movie debut next April, helping keep the series front and center.","While the original game pioneered three-dimensional video games and established enduring action mechanics that still reign over the industry, the new version introduces modest yet welcome mechanical updates. Players can now utilize a manual jump button, a dedicated sprint feature, and a free-rotating camera. These additions replace the old reliance on endless rolling across grassy plains and automatic jumping off ledges. Additionally, the interface incorporates modern touches inspired by 2017's Breath of the Wild, including a pause menu quest log called Threads of Time and a scrolling inventory bar.","Aesthetic transformations are the most striking aspect of the remake, making it the most ornate Zelda game ever made. The kingdom of Hyrule has been enhanced with intricate details, such as hand-stitched, embroidered fabrics on Link's tunic, leather garments, and furry creatures with mosaic wings for fairies. The newly orchestrated soundtrack grants galloping freedom to melodies that were once compressed on Nintendo 64 hardware, featuring tentative brass when locking onto enemies. However, Link's updated character model has sparked debate among critics and fans. With large glassy eyes, a blushing nose, fat cheeks, and porcelain-like skin that reflects light, the hero's design appears notably doll-like and has led some to accuse Nintendo of pursuing a textbook next-gen sheen.","Addressing the stylistic choice, former Nintendo art director Takaya Imamura noted on social media that the design may draw inspiration from creator Shigeru Miyamoto's fondness for traditional Japanese puppet drama, known as ningyogeki. Translator Paul McQuade added that this juvenile, doll-like appearance captures the essence of the forest where children do not grow up, drawing on the vocabulary of dolls used in Shōwa postwar puppet shows aired by NHK. Although some reviewers observed that the dense environments can occasionally overwhelm the eye and complicate navigation—such as in the notoriously fiendish Forest Temple—critics generally agree that the strong foundational design of the original game remains intact, ensuring a polished victory lap for a genre-defining classic."],"facts":[{"fact":"Nintendo is releasing a remake of its 1998 classic The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time for the Nintendo Switch 2 on November 5, 2026.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"The game features a newly orchestrated soundtrack, 4K visuals, and detailed aesthetic updates such as hand-stitched tunics and furry fairies.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Mechanical improvements include a manual jump, a sprint button, and a free-rotating camera, replacing the old automatic jumping and rolling mechanics.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Former art director Takaya Imamura suggested that Link's porcelain-like, doll-like facial features might reflect Shigeru Miyamoto's love of puppet drama.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The release is strategically timed ahead of the upcoming Zelda live-action movie debut in April and avoids direct clashes except for competing with Grand Theft Auto VI.","sources":[1,2]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Nintendo","lemma":"Nintendo","pos":"noun","he":"נינטנדו","name":true},{"text":"preparing","lemma":"prepare","pos":"verb","he":"מתכונן","name":false},{"text":"release","lemma":"release","pos":"verb","he":"להוציא","name":false},{"text":"lavish","lemma":"lavish","pos":"adjective","he":"מפואר","name":false},{"text":"remake","lemma":"remake","pos":"noun","he":"גרסה מחודשת","name":false},{"text":"classic","lemma":"classic","pos":"adjective","he":"קלאסי","name":false},{"text":"video game","lemma":"video game","pos":"noun","he":"משחק וידאו","name":false},{"text":"The Legend of Zelda","lemma":"The Legend of Zelda","pos":"noun","he":"האגדה של זלדה","name":true},{"text":"Ocarina of Time","lemma":"Ocarina